<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">RunLoop</code> is a very fundamental concept in <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">iOS</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">OSX</code> development. This article starts with the source code of <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">CFRunLoop</code> and introduces the concept of <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">RunLoop</code> and its underlying implementation principles. After that, it explains how Apple uses <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">RunLoop</code> in <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">iOS</code> to implement features such as the autorelease pool, delayed callbacks, touch events, and screen refreshes.</p>

