<p>A <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Mach</code> message is actually a binary data packet (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">BLOB</code>). Its header defines the current port <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">local_port</code> and the target port <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">remote_port</code>. Sending and receiving messages are done through the same <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">API</code>, and its <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">option</code> marks the direction of message transfer:</p>

<div class="language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><!-- <td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
